  "question": {
    "html": "<p>P and R are parallel wires carrying the same current into the plane of the paper. P and R are equidistant from a point Q. The line PQ is perpendicular to the line RQ.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The magnetic field due to P at Q is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span>. What is the magnitude of the resultant magnetic field at Q due to both wires?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{X}{2}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\\sqrt{2}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2X\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
